WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.935
-Our next guest is the wife of
the late Senator John McCain

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:04.304
and the chair of the board
of the McCain Institute,

00:00:04.304 --> 00:00:07.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
where she leads the Human
Trafficking Advisory Council

00:00:07.307 --> 00:00:10.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please welcome to the show
Cindy McCain.

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:10.777 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
How are you, Cindy?

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:11.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
I'm well.

00:00:11.745 --> 00:00:13.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you.
Thank you for having me.

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:15.415 line:92%
-It's always lovely to see you

00:00:15.415 --> 00:00:17.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I want to talk about
the fact

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:19.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you are
a lifelong Republican

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:20.253 line:92%
who has endorsed Joe Biden

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:25.892
I did not realize, however, that
Dr. Jill Biden introduced yo

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:29.462 size:81% position:41%
and your late husband,
Senator John McCain.

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:31.398 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes, she did.

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:32.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was fun.
It was in Hawaii.

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:35.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was invited with my parent
to a reception

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:38.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
that was being held
for a group of senators

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:41.241 align:start size:94% position:6%
on their way
through Hawaii to China,

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:42.142 line:92%
and John happened to be there.

00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:45.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
And although I didn't see this
when it initially happened

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:49.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I guess when I came in
the room, he was staring at me

00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:50.884 line:92%
And she said, "Go meet her

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:52.986 line:92%
Go over there and talk to her.

00:00:52.986 --> 00:00:54.854 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So he did.

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:56.289 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And the rest is history.

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:58.792
-Was his --
Did he have a good approach game

00:00:58.792 --> 00:01:00.794 size:88% position:44% line:92%
when he first came over?

00:01:00.794 --> 00:01:02.929 line:92%
Were you interested immediately?

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:03.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
No, I was.

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:06.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, you know --
when he walked over to me, I -

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:09.269 line:92%
"Ooh, this guy's really cute."

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:12.272 size:88% position:44%
And later on that night,
we went and had a drink

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:13.807 line:92%
at the Royal Hawaiian Hotel,

00:01:13.807 --> 00:01:15.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is --
you know, it has tiki --

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:18.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
tiki torches
and everything else going on

00:01:18.078 --> 00:01:20.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then he called me
from China.

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:22.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
He wound up calling me
from China when he got there

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:26.653
So it was -- I guess it was love
at first sight.

00:01:26.653 --> 00:01:27.187 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It was fun.

00:01:27.187 --> 00:01:29.823 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Can you talk a little
about the transition you mad

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:33.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
from, one, sort of privately
supporting Joe Biden

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:37.130 size:81% position:41%
to making the decision
to go public with it?

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:38.098 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:41.000
Well, you know, it was
gradual in some respects.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.735
You know, I, like everyone else,
had watched

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:45.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
what was going on
with this president and with -

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:47.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the actions
that the White House

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.442 line:92%
were taking on various issues.

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:51.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know, it started --
like everyone,

00:01:51.845 --> 00:01:55.782
I spent my day yelling at the TV
when I was watching it.

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:58.118 line:92%
And the final blow for me,

00:01:58.118 --> 00:02:00.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
not only just the lack
of empathy and compassion,

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:06.526 align:start size:94% position:6%
the lack of character,
the absolute unbelievable issu

00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:10.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
of not working in
a bipartisan fashion at all,

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:10.864 line:92%
but the final blow for me

00:02:10.864 --> 00:02:14.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
was when he called
our troops losers and suckers.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:17.437 size:88% position:44%
And I have three members
of my family, two sons

00:02:17.437 --> 00:02:19.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
and a daughter-in-law,
that are serving.

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:21.407 line:92%
And I -- at that point I said,

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:23.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I can sit here
and yell at the TV,

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:24.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
or I can get up
and do something."

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:28.815
And so that's what I did, and
decided to openly endorse him.

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:29.716 line:92%
I am a Republican, though,

00:02:29.716 --> 00:02:31.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I am going
to remain a Republican.

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:35.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So I wonder what you would sa
to other Republicans

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:36.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
whose intention
is to, obviously,

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:39.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
stay loyal to the party,
who are making this decision

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:41.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
between maybe not supporting
the President,

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:45.465 size:84% position:42%
but also being hesitant
to vote for Joe Biden.

00:02:45.465 --> 00:02:46.366 line:92%
Maybe a lot of them would say,

00:02:46.366 --> 00:02:48.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Well, I'm just not
going to vote at all."

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:50.403 line:92%
What would you say to them

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:54.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, that's what I'm tryin
to help avoid, obviously.

00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:55.408 line:92%
Judging by the outcome of all --

00:02:55.408 --> 00:03:00.580
Now what? 67 million early
ballots have been turned in.

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:02.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think we're not going to
have a problem

00:03:02.415 --> 00:03:03.883 size:84% position:42% line:92%
with people not voting.

00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:07.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
But what I do want people
to realize, look, this is --

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:10.390 size:84% position:42%
you know, I don't agree
with Joe on everything.

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:11.824 line:92%
I believe that Joe will work

00:03:11.824 --> 00:03:16.529
in a bipartisan fashion, though,
to reach common ground

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:18.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
and work on issues
that are important for us.

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:22.969
And more importantly, I mean
a large part of this is the fact

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:26.306 line:92%
that Joe has a COVID plan.

00:03:26.306 --> 00:03:27.540 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Unlike the White House

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:30.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the rest of the members,
he believes it's real.

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:35.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
He believes and talks
to the scientists involved

00:03:35.215 --> 00:03:37.116 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And now, you know,

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:39.485 size:78% position:39%
it's time that we put
his plan into action.

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:42.589 size:84% position:42%
It's things like that
that I tell Republicans

00:03:42.589 --> 00:03:43.790 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
when they ask me.

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:45.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, it's --
I'm tired of some --

00:03:45.825 --> 00:03:49.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
of my president
not having my back on things

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:50.330 size:78% position:39% line:92%
And more importantly,

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:54.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
not having our country's
back internationally.

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:57.604 size:75% position:38%
You know, we've left
our allies behind.

00:03:57.604 --> 00:03:59.973 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We've left our --

00:03:59.973 --> 00:04:02.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
We've withdrawn
from treaties, et cetera.

00:04:02.976 --> 00:04:06.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, our country is not wel
respected overseas

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:07.180 size:81% position:41% line:92%
either in all of this.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:09.315 line:92%
There's a lot at stake here.

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:13.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Your husband was attacked
by the President

00:04:13.186 --> 00:04:16.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
in his trademark
style of cruelty,

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:20.159 align:start size:94% position:6%
not only when he was alive
but after he passed.

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:24.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you think John would
enjoy the fact

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:26.165 line:92%
that he's still taking up

00:04:26.165 --> 00:04:29.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
so much head space
of the President?

00:04:29.102 --> 00:04:33.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our family's talked
about that a little bit.

00:04:33.039 --> 00:04:34.140 line:92%
I know one thing for sure.

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:37.343
John would be very disappointe
in what's going on right now

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:41.447
This is not -- This was not,
you know, what he believed in,

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:45.051 size:81% position:41%
nor would he ever have
wanted to ever happen.

00:04:45.051 --> 00:04:47.920
I think the fact that he i
taking up head space, though

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:51.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
is kind of hilarious
on occasion.

00:04:51.691 --> 00:04:56.729
-You mentioned the lack of
the sort of COVID response plan.

00:04:56.729 --> 00:04:59.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think that maybe
runs parallel

00:04:59.632 --> 00:05:01.668 line:92%
with Senator McCain's decision

00:05:01.668 --> 00:05:05.104 size:88% position:44%
to give the thumbs-down
to the Obamacare repeal.

00:05:05.104 --> 00:05:08.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
It wasn't that he was
a great fan of Obamacare,

00:05:08.341 --> 00:05:09.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
but he recognized
in the moment

00:05:09.809 --> 00:05:11.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
that there was not
a replacement.

00:05:11.577 --> 00:05:14.213
Did you talk to him a great deal
about that moment

00:05:14.213 --> 00:05:17.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
when he, you know,
now quite significantly,

00:05:17.116 --> 00:05:18.384 size:78% position:39% line:92%
broke with his party?

00:05:18.384 --> 00:05:21.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
We talked about it beforehand.

00:05:21.854 --> 00:05:24.390 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know --
things like that, I --

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:27.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
To give you a little
behind-the-scenes thing,

00:05:27.527 --> 00:05:30.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lot was going on
in the cloakroom behind.

00:05:30.129 --> 00:05:32.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
The Vice President
was back there.

00:05:32.332 --> 00:05:35.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
The governor of Arizona,
I believe, was on the phone.

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:38.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
They were lobbying
my husband pretty hard.

00:05:38.671 --> 00:05:42.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
But the one thing he knew
is that we could not do away

00:05:42.475 --> 00:05:46.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
with Obamacare without a pla
on the other side

00:05:46.546 --> 00:05:47.447 size:81% position:41% line:92%
and there was no plan.

00:05:47.447 --> 00:05:50.750 size:84% position:42%
So he had, in his mind,
and I believe rightly,

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:54.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
as he agreed,
it was the right thing to do

00:05:54.754 --> 00:05:56.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
These kinds of votes
and decisions,

00:05:56.756 --> 00:05:57.824 line:92%
you know, you don't always -

00:05:57.824 --> 00:06:01.294
you're not always popular
when you make the right decision

00:06:01.294 --> 00:06:03.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
and John knew that,
and John abided by it.

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:06.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm glad he did
what he did. I really am.

00:06:06.966 --> 00:06:10.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
But they did put a full-cour
press on him.

00:06:10.036 --> 00:06:12.138
-Obviously right now in th
last week with the campaign,

00:06:12.138 --> 00:06:15.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
you've been through this -
-Crazy time right now.

00:06:15.641 --> 00:06:18.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
Last week of the campaign
is nuts.

00:06:18.945 --> 00:06:20.713 line:92%
-What is the energy like?

00:06:20.713 --> 00:06:22.515 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, it's wild.

00:06:22.515 --> 00:06:23.449 size:81% position:41% line:92%
No one gets any sleep.

00:06:23.449 --> 00:06:26.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everyone's really
running on coffee

00:06:26.185 --> 00:06:28.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
and probably
a little liquor, too.

00:06:28.154 --> 00:06:31.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's just, you know,
it's nonstop.

00:06:31.391 --> 00:06:34.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
These last seven days
are nonstop

00:06:34.427 --> 00:06:36.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you've got to get
to the finish line.

00:06:36.095 --> 00:06:41.467 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We crossed paths during
the last seven days in 2008.

00:06:41.467 --> 00:06:42.869 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We did.
-For all your accomplishments,

00:06:42.869 --> 00:06:46.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're also a very
accomplished sketch actor.

00:06:46.038 --> 00:06:47.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-Here you are.

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:49.942 line:92%
This was a QVC sketch we did

00:06:49.942 --> 00:06:51.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
where, in the final days
of the campaign,

00:06:51.611 --> 00:06:53.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
the Senator was trying
to raise some campaign funds

00:06:53.846 --> 00:06:57.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you did a very good jo
in the sketch.

00:06:57.116 --> 00:06:59.218 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you have fond memories
of that night?

00:06:59.218 --> 00:07:01.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I do.
You know, there -- a lot of --

00:07:01.921 --> 00:07:04.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
people say, "Well, aren't
campaigns hard?"

00:07:04.123 --> 00:07:04.957 size:78% position:39% line:92%
and all those things.

00:07:04.957 --> 00:07:07.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
And there are some
very hard moments.

00:07:07.026 --> 00:07:09.962 align:start size:94% position:6%
But doing "SNL"
was a fun moment.

00:07:09.962 --> 00:07:11.931
And as you know,
my husband did it several times.

00:07:11.931 --> 00:07:15.268 size:84% position:42%
And I was just grateful
to be a part of that.

00:07:15.268 --> 00:07:17.203 line:92%
I had a great time. It was fun

00:07:17.203 --> 00:07:21.040 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Another thing that bonded
your family with the Bidens is

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:24.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you mentioned it earlier
military service.

00:07:24.744 --> 00:07:27.847
You know, obviously it's bee
true of both your families

00:07:27.847 --> 00:07:33.019
Is that something that Joh
and Joe would speak about often?

00:07:33.019 --> 00:07:33.686 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Often, yes.

00:07:33.686 --> 00:07:35.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, we --
our sons both left

00:07:35.955 --> 00:07:37.824 line:92%
at about the same time for Iraq.

00:07:37.824 --> 00:07:40.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, here, Joe was runnin
for vice president,

00:07:40.626 --> 00:07:42.128 align:start size:94% position:6%
my husband
was running for president,

00:07:42.128 --> 00:07:46.899
and we both had two sons serving
in Iraq at the same time.

00:07:46.899 --> 00:07:49.502 size:84% position:42%
You know, it's not only
a bonding experience

00:07:49.502 --> 00:07:52.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the families,
but it made both families --

00:07:52.805 --> 00:07:55.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
ours, and of course
the Biden family,

00:07:55.608 --> 00:07:58.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
understand what the families
of troops

00:07:58.144 --> 00:07:59.879 line:92%
go through when they deploy.

00:07:59.879 --> 00:08:01.047 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I mean, it's hard.

00:08:01.047 --> 00:08:04.584 size:84% position:42%
And so I -- so he has
a different perspective

00:08:04.584 --> 00:08:06.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
and a good perspective
on what it means

00:08:06.853 --> 00:08:08.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
to serve your country
in the military

00:08:08.521 --> 00:08:10.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the effect
it has on families.

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:12.792 align:start size:94% position:6%
But more importantly,
you know, we have that --

00:08:12.792 --> 00:08:14.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
that commonality,
but as you know,

00:08:14.594 --> 00:08:19.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
we have the commonality
of glioblastoma,

00:08:19.398 --> 00:08:20.867 line:92%
which hit both of our families

00:08:20.867 --> 00:08:24.403
And so it would be hard
to separate the Biden and McCain

00:08:24.403 --> 00:08:25.838 size:84% position:42% line:92%
family in years to come

00:08:25.838 --> 00:08:27.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
because we're just
too good of friends.

00:08:27.673 --> 00:08:33.045
-You also have spoken of forme
Vice President Biden's empathy

00:08:33.045 --> 00:08:34.881 line:92%
And I guess that was on display.

00:08:34.881 --> 00:08:39.452
He did come and visit your
husband in the final days, yeah?

00:08:39.452 --> 00:08:40.620 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-He did. He came out.

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:42.255 line:92%
My husband was still alert

00:08:42.255 --> 00:08:43.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
a little bit --
he wasn't too alert,

00:08:43.556 --> 00:08:46.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
but he was alert and awake
and recognized Joe

00:08:46.959 --> 00:08:48.394 line:92%
and could talk a little bit.

00:08:48.394 --> 00:08:52.665 size:84% position:42%
And Joe had just been
through this with Beau.

00:08:52.665 --> 00:08:54.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, he'd just been
through it.

00:08:54.901 --> 00:08:58.371 line:92%
And here he is, out in Arizona

00:08:58.371 --> 00:09:00.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
Number one,
joking like crazy with John.

00:09:00.973 --> 00:09:02.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
John was laughing
as best he could.

00:09:02.608 --> 00:09:07.647
I mean, it was fun to watc
and just the normal things

